  "findings": [
    "AbstractMessage#addLifeEvent attaches the event first and records independent activate/deactivate type flags for matching self participants. Step1Message adds the two lifecycle deltas independently so they cancel when both are set. Rust now retains both flags and its legacy shared geometry consumes them; four primary legacy controls pass.",
    "The four matching Teoz controls fail by30px because the shared lifecycle scheduler still inserts a legacy combined row and the Teoz self painter reads only shorthand Message.activation. The fresh focused both-flag/direction controls also reveal the shared reverse-envelope failure. Correct flag aggregation is not independently accepted while these consumers remain inconsistent.",
    "The original maker attached matrices (48+48) reproduce as passing, but they do not cover the independent engine/direction/standalone-note combinations generated here.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
